### Third-Party Licenses & Attributions

The web template bundled in `skills/academic-project-page/template/` and `skills/academic-project-page/static/` is adapted from the Academic Project Page Template (https://github.com/eliahuhorwitz/Academic-project-page-template) by Eliahu Horwitz, which is itself adapted from the Nerfies project page (https://github.com/nerfies/nerfies.github.io) by Keunhong Park, Utkarsh Sinha, Jonathan T. Barron, Sofien Bouaziz, Dan B Goldman, Steven M. Seitz, and Ricardo Martin-Brualla. No media from either project is included.

Both website templates are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Any project page generated using this template must retain the attribution to both templates in the website footer, as required by the CC BY-SA 4.0 license.

Bundled libraries keep their own license headers: Bulma (MIT) in `static/css/bulma.min.css`, and Font Awesome Free (icons CC BY 4.0, code MIT) in `static/js/fontawesome.all.min.js`.

The fictional evaluation kit in `eval-kit/` (generator output and kits) is dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/). The Latin Modern fonts in `eval-kit/generator/fonts/` are distributed under the GUST Font License; see the license and notice files in that folder.
